# The Debian packages of the environment distributions are tested in, for
# the image around gperl and for the image around perl itself alike: what
# differs between the two is the interpreter, nothing else.

# The C toolchain and the tools build scripts run.
build-essential ca-certificates curl git patch pkg-config unzip bzip2 xz-utils
cmake graphviz protobuf-compiler

# More tools that build scripts and test suites run, as CPAN Testers
# machines commonly have them: GNU libtool for bundled autotools builds
# (Alien-libtickit, Linux-Seccomp), file (libtool's configure, and tests
# that run it: Alien-SNMP, GraphViz-Graph, Lingua-YALI, Data-Table-Text),
# a Fortran compiler for ExtUtils::F77 (ExtUtils-F77, PDL-Opt-QP), rsync,
# ip and ping (File-Rsync, Sys-HostIP, Net-Address-Ethernet,
# Net-Ping-External), vim (Text-VimColor, and vi for Proc-InvokeEditor),
# pdfimages (PDF-GetImages), node (Alien-Nodejs uses the system one),
# tclsh (Tcl), an English word list (Text-Aspell, and Dezi through
# LucyX::Suggester), and a virtual X display for the test phase (xvfb-run,
# with xauth; Test-NeedsDisplay, Tk widgets, Prima, ...).
#
# The cost of libtool: with Debian's libtool, Alien::libtool is a system
# install, and Alien-SeqAlignment-parasail's autoreconf through the
# share-built Alien::automake (Debian's automake is too old for it) then
# misses libtool.m4 ("Libtool library used but 'LIBTOOL' is undefined");
# without the package it passes. libtool gains more than that one:
# Alien-libtickit and the Tickit distributions behind it, and
# Sys-Linux-Syscall-Execve.
libtool libtool-bin file gfortran rsync iproute2 iputils-ping vim
poppler-utils nodejs tcl xvfb xauth aspell-en

# setcap, with which user.sh takes the file capabilities off programs (they
# cannot be run in a container without capabilities).
libcap2-bin

# Locales named *.UTF-8 (en_US.UTF-8, fr_FR.UTF-8, ...): the base image has
# only C.utf8, which distributions looking for a "UTF-8" locale do not
# accept (SWISH-3 and what depends on it, Unicode-Block,
# Zonemaster-Backend).
locales-all

# The network databases (/etc/services, /etc/protocols, ...): the official
# perl image's base has them and debian:bookworm-slim does not, so
# getservbyname and getprotobyname answered differently in the two images.
netbase

