# The MySQL 8 client library is not a Debian package (bookworm has
# MariaDB's): mysql.sh installs Oracle's. MariaDB's library stays
# (libmariadb-dev, mariadb_config) for the distributions that bind to it;
# its MySQL compatibility layer, libmariadb-dev-compat, is left out: its
# /usr/include/mysql is a link to MariaDB's headers, which Oracle's would
# be written over, and its mysql_config, libmysqlclient.so and
# mysqlclient.pc name MariaDB's library under MySQL's names.
